---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import AchList from '../components/AchList.astro';
import Ref from '../components/Ref.astro';
import { achievements, listMeta } from '../lib/site';

const visible = listMeta.total - listMeta.hidden;
---

<Base
  title="Stranger Than Heaven Achievements: All 59, with Tracker"
  description="Every Stranger Than Heaven achievement and trophy in one checklist: 59 entries by category and act, saved on your device, with hidden story names masked."
  path="/achievements/"
>
  <h1>Stranger Than Heaven achievements: all {listMeta.total}, with a tracker</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Tick each one as you earn it. Your progress is saved in this browser, and the {listMeta.hidden} story achievements
    that Steam hides stay masked until you choose to see their names.
  </p>
  <p class="notice">
    <strong>Pre-release list.</strong> These {listMeta.total} entries surfaced on 8 and 9 September 2026, when achievement
    data for unreleased games turned out to be readable through Steam. SEGA has not confirmed the list and it can
    change before launch.
    PlayStation trophies normally match. <a href="#where">Where it came from</a>.
  </p>

  <AchList items={achievements} mode="full" />

  <h2>What finishing the list takes</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Reading the highest step of each chain, a full clear means:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>the whole main story, five acts;</li>
      <li>every substory in all five cities, and the Showbiz story in all five;</li>
      <li>30 livelihood missions, 50 shows, 10 different singers and 50 ideas;</li>
      <li>1,000 enemies defeated, 70 Arts abilities, and Health and Willpower both at level 50;</li>
      <li>100 kinds of weapon, 30 forges, one weapon forged and awakened to its limit, and proficiency level 10 with one weapon and with bare hands;</li>
      <li>the act-specific job in each of Acts 1 to 4;</li>
      <li>20 developed photos, 20 hand-rolled cigarettes, 70 menko cards and beigoma tops, and 10 different minigames.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Nothing on the list mentions a difficulty setting, a time limit or anything online
      <Ref ids="list" />.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Can you miss any of them?</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Nobody outside SEGA knows yet. Three of the categories are tied to a single act: the substories, the
      Showbiz story and the act-specific job each name their act, and every act is a different city in a different
      decade. Whether the game lets you go back to an earlier act has not been said.
    </p>
    <p>
      Until that is known, the cautious way to play is to clear an act's own list before finishing its last chapter.
      The <a href="/acts/">act pages</a> show that short list for each city. This page will be updated as soon as the
      answer is confirmed.
    </p>
    <p>
      One hint that some content is tied to its era: the developers have said certain minigames exist only in the
      Kokura period <Ref ids="automaton" />. The minigame achievement asks for any 10 different ones, so it does not
      depend on a particular game, but it is a reason to try what each city offers while you are there.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>What the list suggests about the game</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>These are readings of the list, not announcements:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Five acts, one per city. Acts 1 to 4 each have an entry for Chapter 1, for Chapter 2 and for finishing the act. Act 5 has one for Chapter 1 and one for the final chapter.</li>
      <li>Three kinds of side content run alongside the story: substories, a Showbiz story in every act, and livelihood missions.</li>
      <li>Fighting has more to grow than fists: Arts abilities, Health and Willpower levels, weapon proficiency, and weapons that are forged and then awakened.</li>
      <li>There are at least 10 minigames, and things to collect: menko cards and beigoma tops, both old Japanese children's games.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>More on each system, and which parts SEGA has described itself, is on the <a href="/gameplay/">gameplay page</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="where">Where the list came from</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Overnight on 8 and 9 September 2026, achievement lists for dozens of unreleased Steam games appeared on
      Exophase, a site that tracks achievements by scanning Steam automatically. Its owner said the data should have
      been private and was reachable through Steam's API, which pointed to a mistake on Valve's side
      <Ref ids="leak" />. Stranger Than Heaven was among the games. Trophy site PowerPyx published the 59 entries on
      9 September <Ref ids="list" />, and a second write-up counted {visible} visible entries and
      {listMeta.hidden} hidden ones <Ref ids="list-2" />.
    </p>
    <p>
      The names on this page are the reported names. The requirements are restated in our own words from those two
      copies, which agree on every number. Steam's store page does not show an achievement list at the moment
      (checked {listMeta.checked}) <Ref ids="steam" />.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>About spoilers</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      The {listMeta.hidden} hidden entries are all main-story achievements, one for each chapter and act. Their
      requirements give nothing away, so those are shown. Their names might hint at the story, so they are masked
      until you tick "Show hidden achievement names". The choice is remembered on this device.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
